.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RAND_GET0_PRIMARY 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RAND_get0_primary ,
.Nm RAND_get0_public ,
.Nm RAND_get0_private ,
.Nm RAND_set0_public ,
.Nm RAND_set0_private
.Nd get access to the global EVP_RAND_CTX instances
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rand.h
.Ft EVP_RAND_CTX *
.Fo RAND_get0_primary
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_RAND_CTX *
.Fo RAND_get0_public
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_RAND_CTX *
.Fo RAND_get0_private
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_set0_public
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "EVP_RAND_CTX *rand"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_set0_private
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "EVP_RAND_CTX *rand"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The default RAND API implementation
.Xr (RAND_OpenSSL 3 )
utilizes three shared DRBG instances which are accessed via the RAND
API:
.Pp
The
.Em public
and
.Em private
DRBG are thread-local instances, which are used by
.Xr RAND_bytes 3
and
.Xr RAND_priv_bytes 3 ,
respectively.
The
.Em primary
DRBG is a global instance, which is not intended to be used directly,
but is used internally to reseed the other two instances.
.Pp
The three get functions provide access to the shared DRBG instances.
.Pp
The two set functions allow the public and private DRBG instances to be
replaced by another random number generator.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn RAND_get0_primary
returns a pointer to the
.Em primary
DRBG instance for the given OSSL_LIB_CTX
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Fn RAND_get0_public
returns a pointer to the
.Em public
DRBG instance for the given OSSL_LIB_CTX
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Fn RAND_get0_private
returns a pointer to the
.Em private
DRBG instance for the given OSSL_LIB_CTX
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Fn RAND_set0_public
and
.Fn RAND_set0_private
return 1 on success and 0 on error.
.Sh NOTES
It is not thread-safe to access the
.Em primary
DRBG instance.
The
.Em public
and
.Em private
DRBG instance can be accessed safely, because they are thread-local.
Note however, that changes to these two instances apply only to the
current thread.
.Pp
For that reason it is recommended not to change the settings of these
three instances directly.
Instead, an application should change the default settings for new DRBG
instances at initialization time, before creating additional threads.
.Pp
During initialization, it is possible to change the reseed interval and
reseed time interval.
It is also possible to exchange the reseeding callbacks entirely.
.Pp
To set the type of DRBG that will be instantiated, use the
.Xr RAND_set_DRBG_type 3
call before accessing the random number generation infrastructure.
.Pp
The two set functions, operate on the current thread.
If you want to use the same random number generator across all threads,
each thread must individually call the set functions.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 ,
.Xr RAND_set_DRBG_type 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn RAND_set0_public
and
.Fn RAND_set0_private
were added in OpenSSL 3.1.
.Pp
The remaining functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
